{
  "contract": "routes.v1",
  "domain": "agent",
  "owner": "core/agent",
  "edge": "gateway",
  "note": "The agent control plane. ABSENT in the no-agents profile (PRD decision 40.6) \u2014 these rows and the routes that carry them are simply not there, so a request 404s. The edge registers them from this file: `forward` maps /agent/<path> onto agent-api's /api/<path>, every row but the catch-all is a route of its own (`stream` relays server-sent events), `delegation` admits a worker's own delegation token \u2014 on the friction report its harness files, and nowhere else \u2014 and `mcp_reentry` admits it on the MCP's re-entry: one row per route a tool in mcp.tools.v1.json calls, and no other.",
